Upstream: https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco_warp/tree/v0.0.2

Modified source/algorithm origins:
- _src/collision_primitive.py: static contact parameter priority/solmix rules.
- _src/collision_primitive_core.py: plane-sphere distance/contact midpoint.
- _src/constraint.py: _update_efc_row impedance, regularization and reference acceleration.
- _src/forward.py: Euler velocity/position order and implicit joint damping.
- _src/math.py: local-angular-velocity quaternion integration.

Phymeo changes: independent TYX kernels/resources and model admission,
constant full mass operators for all-prismatic trees/centered isotropic free body,
closed-form single frictionless normal QP, transactional publication and
explicit capability/precision diagnostics. No Warp kernel or runtime executes
through this package. This is a limited port, not complete MuJoCo support.

Contact priority/direct-reference selection follows MuJoCo 3.3.7
src/engine/engine_collision_driver.c::mj_contactParam, correcting a v0.0.2
Warp discrepancy for unequal priorities with positive/direct solref.

Decreasing and zero-width impedance and denominator guards follow MuJoCo
3.3.7 src/engine/engine_core_constraint.c::getimpedance/mj_makeImpedance.
Detection includes the exact margin boundary, retaining inactive contact sites.

T1 fixed-root hinge/slide tree port (_tree_model.py/_tree_kernels.py/_tree_device.py):
source field and algorithm references include v0.0.2 smooth.py kinematics/com_vel/
crb/rne, passive.py scalar spring/damper, and scalar transmission/Euler.
The TYX rewrite uses world-origin motion recursion, COM Jacobian assembly and
per-step full mass/bias with bounded dense Cholesky; it does not freeze a
configuration-specific MuJoCo mass or invoke Warp/CPU dynamics at each step.
Disabled actuator force clamping follows CPU MuJoCo 3.3.7 before gear aggregation.

T2 free-root tree port (_floating_model.py/_floating_kernels.py/_floating_device.py):
the same v0.0.2 smooth/passive/forward algorithms are rewritten for a native
free root and up to 29 scalar joints, including root-COM offsets and the full
root/joint inertia coupling. Root linear velocity is world-frame and angular
velocity is root-local; quaternion integration uses a right local increment.
Coordinate, Jacobian and Euler semantics are checked against MuJoCo 3.3.7
engine_core_smooth.c, engine_util_spatial.c and engine_forward.c.
The bounded TYX dense solve and transactional device resources are independent;
CPU MuJoCo compiles the model but does not execute these per-step dynamics.
Free-joint springs and possible contacts in this tree domain remain unsupported.
